cac:TenderingProcess><cac:ProcurementProject><cbc:ID>1</cbc:ID><cbc:Name languageID="DEU">Silicon Austria Labs – Photonic debonder (manual/ semi-automated)</cbc:Name><cbc:Description languageID="DEU">The aim of this procurement procedure is to award the contract to the best bidder identified during the procurement procedure for the supply, installation, commissioning as well as optional services (after warranty) of a Photonic debonder (manual/ semi-automated) for Silicon Austria Labs GmbH.</cbc:Description><cbc:ProcurementTypeCode listName="contract-nature">supplies</cbc:ProcurementTypeCode><cbc:Note languageID="DEU">The information under point “Duration of the contract, framework agreement or dynamic procurement system” was only provided because it is a mandatory field. In fact, a supply contract is concluded, which generally ends with the delivery, installation, commissioning, training and acceptance. The actual term will therefore only be determined after installation, commissioning and acceptance. Regarding the point “Maximum number of applicants to be invited to the second phase”, it is noted that if one (or more) candidate achieves the same score as the third-ranked candidate according to the selection criteria, all candidates with this score will be admitted to the second stage, regardless of how many there are. The information under point "Minimum number of participants to be invited to the second phase" was only provided because it is a mandatory field. If fewer than three requests to participate are received from suitable candidates, these candidates will be admitted to the second stage. The information under point “Variants”, it is noted that proposals for changes can be attached to the offer in accordance with point 6.2.2 - Part A. With regard to “Language of submission”, it is noted that submissions can be made in German and English. For technical reasons, it is not possible to state this.</cbc:Note><cbc:SMESuitableIndicator>true</cbc:SMESuitableIndicat